-- dsssb-je-mts-1260-posts-20261112 (English 1823 words; Nepali 1089 words)
INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt")
VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'dsssb-je-mts-1260-posts-20261112', 'asia', 'India',
'DSSSB JE MTS Recruitment 2026: 1,260 Posts, Apply from 12 November',
'डीएसएसएसबी जेई एमटीएस भर्ती २०२६: १,२६० पद, आवेदन १२ नोभेम्बरदेखि',
'Delhi Subordinate Services Selection Board has opened 1,260 DSSSB JE MTS posts under Advertisement No. 06/2026. Apply online at dsssbonline.nic.in from 12 November 2026 noon to 11 December 2026; Junior Engineer has 185 posts and Multi-Tasking Staff has 1,075 posts.',
'दिल्ली अधीनस्थ सेवा चयन बोर्डले विज्ञापन नं. ०६/२०२६ अन्तर्गत डीएसएसएसबी जेई एमटीएसका १,२६० पद खोलेको छ। आवेदन १२ नोभेम्बर २०२६ दिउँसो १२ बजेदेखि ११ डिसेम्बर २०२६ सम्म dsssbonline.nic.in बाट अनलाइन मात्र दिन सकिन्छ; जुनियर इन्जिनियर १८५ पद र मल्टी-टास्किङ स्टाफ १,०७५ पद छन्।',
$$<p>The Delhi Subordinate Services Selection Board has opened 1,260 DSSSB JE MTS posts under Advertisement No. 06/2026, and the online form opens today, 12 November 2026 at 12:00 noon, and runs to 11 December 2026, 11:59 PM. The two groups are Junior Engineer (Electric) / Junior Engineer (Electrical), post code 809/26, with 185 posts, and Multi-Tasking Staff, post code 810/26, with 1,075 posts, including Multi-Tasking Staff – Aaya (Female). The recruitment covers departments and local bodies under the Government of NCT of Delhi, and the selection is through a computer based written examination. The vacancies are tentative, based on inputs from the indenting departments, so the final figure can still change.</p>
<table><tr><th>At a glance</th><th>DSSSB JE MTS Recruitment 2026</th></tr><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>Delhi Subordinate Services Selection Board (DSSSB)</td></tr><tr><td>Notification</td><td>Advertisement No. 06/2026, Combined Examinations 2026, dated 6 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Posts</td><td>Junior Engineer 809/26; Multi-Tasking Staff 810/26</td></tr><tr><td>Total seats</td><td>1,260 (tentative)</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>12 November 2026 (12:00 noon) to 11 December 2026 (11:59 PM)</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online only at dsssbonline.nic.in</td></tr><tr><td>Application fee</td><td>Rs 100; exempt for women, SC, ST, PwBD and ex-servicemen</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>JE: degree or diploma in Electrical Engineering; MTS: Matriculation (10th pass)</td></tr><tr><td>Age limit</td><td>18 to 27 years for most posts; 18 to 32 for Junior Engineer in NDMC; counted as on 11 December 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>JE: Pay Level 6 or 8, Rs 35,400 to Rs 1,51,100; MTS: Pay Level 1, Rs 18,000 to Rs 56,900</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>JE: Two Tier written examination; MTS: One Tier written examination</td></tr><tr><td>Exam date</td><td>Not announced</td></tr></table>
<h2>DSSSB JE MTS posts, department by department</h2>
<p>The 185 Junior Engineer posts sit in five departments: Delhi Transco 75, NDMC 67, MCD 26, DUSIB 14 and DAMB 3.</p>
<table><tr><th>Junior Engineer department</th><th>Seats</th></tr><tr><td>Delhi Transco Limited</td><td>75</td></tr><tr><td>New Delhi Municipal Council (NDMC)</td><td>67</td></tr><tr><td>Municipal Corporation of Delhi (MCD)</td><td>26</td></tr><tr><td>Delhi Urban Shelter Improvement Board (DUSIB)</td><td>14</td></tr><tr><td>Delhi Agricultural Marketing Board (DAMB)</td><td>3</td></tr></table>
<p>The 1,075 Multi-Tasking Staff posts sit in nine departments, and the Directorate of Education takes almost all of them: 757 General Duty and 239 Aaya (Female). The rest are Trade and Taxes 26, DUSIB 20, Weights and Measures 19, Land and Building 7, Higher Education 3, Principal Accounts Office 2 and the Chief Electoral Officer 2.</p>
<table><tr><th>Multi-Tasking Staff department</th><th>Seats</th></tr><tr><td>Directorate of Education – General Duty</td><td>757</td></tr><tr><td>Directorate of Education – Aaya (Female)</td><td>239</td></tr><tr><td>Department of Trade and Taxes</td><td>26</td></tr><tr><td>Delhi Urban Shelter Improvement Board</td><td>20</td></tr><tr><td>Weights and Measures Department</td><td>19</td></tr><tr><td>Land and Building Department</td><td>7</td></tr><tr><td>Directorate of Higher Education</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>Principal Accounts Office</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Chief Electoral Officer</td><td>2</td></tr></table>
<p>The category split is 537 UR, 325 OBC, 181 SC, 94 ST and 123 EWS, with 52 PwBD, 107 ex-serviceman and 52 sportsperson seats. The warning under the table matters: the vacancies are tentative, so they may increase, decrease or become nil before the process ends.</p>
<h2>Who can apply</h2>
<p>For Junior Engineer, the essential qualification is a degree or diploma in Electrical Engineering, with the detail varying by department. NDMC and MCD accept a degree, or a diploma with two years of professional experience. Delhi Agricultural Marketing Board needs a diploma with two years of electrical installation or maintenance work. Delhi Transco accepts a degree or diploma with no experience required, and DUSIB needs a diploma. The pay reflects that split: Delhi Transco pays Pay Level 8, from Rs 52,000 to Rs 1,51,100, while NDMC, MCD and DUSIB pay Pay Level 6, from Rs 35,400 to Rs 1,12,400.</p>
<p>For Multi-Tasking Staff, the essential qualification is Matriculation or an equivalent pass from a recognised board; DUSIB also accepts an Industrial Training Institute pass. No experience is required for any MTS post, and the pay is Pay Level 1, from Rs 18,000 to Rs 56,900, in Group C.</p>
<p>The age limit is 18 to 27 years for most posts, including all MTS posts. The exception is Junior Engineer in NDMC, where the limit is 18 to 32 years. Departmental candidates can get relaxation up to 40 years for MTS posts, and category-wise age relaxation is given in para 8 of the advertisement. The crucial date for qualification, age and experience is 11 December 2026, the closing date of the application. Multi-Tasking Staff – Aaya is for women candidates only, and conditions vary by department, so check the post you want in the advertisement before you apply.</p>
<h2>The fee, and who does not pay</h2>
<p>The application fee is Rs 100, and women candidates and candidates from SC, ST, PwBD and ex-serviceman categories are exempt. Pay online only, through SBI e-pay — no other mode is accepted, and a payment made by another route stands forfeited. The fee, once paid, will not be refunded. Ex-servicemen who have already secured civil employment under the Central Government or the Government of NCT of Delhi after availing re-employment benefits are not eligible for the fee concession.</p>
<h2>How the selection works</h2>
<p>Junior Engineer has a Two Tier (Technical) examination and Multi-Tasking Staff a One Tier (General) examination, separate for each post code. Tier-I for Junior Engineer is a two-hour paper of 200 questions for 200 marks: Section A carries 100 marks across General Awareness, General Intelligence and Reasoning, Arithmetical and Numerical Ability, Hindi and English, at 20 marks each, and Section B carries 100 marks from the subject concerned. Tier-I is only qualifying and is used to shortlist candidates for Tier-II. Tier-II is also two hours, with 150 questions for 200 marks: Part I has 100 one-mark questions covering the syllabus of the qualifying subject, and Part II has 50 two-mark questions testing the application of concepts and problem solving. The final merit list comes from Tier-II.</p>
<p>The MTS paper is a single two-hour tier of 200 questions for 200 marks, with five sections of 40 marks each: General Awareness, General Intelligence and Reasoning, Arithmetical and Numerical Ability, Hindi and English, and the final merit list comes from the marks in that paper.</p>
<p>There is negative marking: 0.25 marks for each wrong answer to a one-mark question, and 0.50 marks for each wrong answer to a two-mark question. The minimum qualifying marks are 40 percent for General and EWS candidates, 35 percent for OBC (Delhi) candidates and 30 percent for SC, ST and PwBD candidates, with a 5 percent relaxation for ex-servicemen, subject to a minimum of 30 percent. The questions are bilingual in Hindi and English, except for the language papers. A skill, endurance, driving or trade test will be taken as per the requirement of the job, and candidates must submit department and post preferences when e-dossiers are called, with at least one preference compulsory.</p>
<h2>How to apply</h2>
<p>Apply online only at dsssbonline.nic.in. The window opens on 12 November 2026 at 12:00 noon and closes on 11 December 2026 at 11:59 PM, when the link will be disabled. No other mode is accepted, and applications sent by post, by hand or by email will not be considered. Submit the form well before the closing date: the Board warns that heavy load on the website in the closing days can stop a candidate from logging in. Check every field before submission, because no change or correction, including a change of category, is entertained after the form is submitted. Keep your registration details, the payment receipt and a copy of the submitted form.</p>
<p>Another large recruitment is open at the same time: <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/rrb-ntpc-undergraduate-1688-posts-20261109">RRB NTPC Undergraduate has opened 1,688 clerk posts for 12th pass candidates</a>, and applications there close on 13 November, so candidates eligible for both should plan the two deadlines together. <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/rrb-isolated-categories-191-posts-20261109">RRB Isolated Categories has 191 posts with applications open till 4 December</a> for graduates looking for a longer window.</p>
<h2>What the notification does not say</h2>
<p>The notification names no examination date. The Board says the date will be intimated in due course, only through its website, so any other date printed elsewhere is not from the notification. It does not say how many posts will finally be filled, because the 1,260 vacancies are tentative. It does not give a final joining date, because that follows the examination and document verification. It does not spell out which posts will carry a skill test or trade test, and the category-wise age relaxation table sits in para 8 of the advertisement, so check it there rather than trusting a summary. The examination scheme can also be changed by the Board at any time before the examination.</p>
<p>Never pay anyone who promises to get you a seat. Genuine recruitment never charges a fee beyond what the notification itself names, and this advertisement names Rs 100 only, payable through SBI e-pay, with women, SC, ST, PwBD and ex-serviceman candidates exempt.</p>
<p>Sources: Delhi Subordinate Services Selection Board, Advertisement No. 06/2026 (Combined Examinations, 2026), File No. F.1(449)/P&amp;P/DSSSB/2026/Advt./5183, dated 6 November 2026. The figures above were verified directly from the official advertisement PDF on dsssb.delhi.gov.in, and cross-checked against Examaalay and FreeJobAlert, which agree on the total, the window, the fee and the examination scheme. The examination date is not announced, and the vacancies are tentative. Apply only through dsssbonline.nic.in.</p>$$,
